# cavekit-find-on-page.md R2, R5 (T-678): the match on the dark band is drawn so it is seen; the bar opened again on
# the same page offers the last word selected, so the next word typed replaces it.
id: find-reopen
section: Find on page
item: Find on Page's match on a dark band is seen (the shot), and the bar opened again offers the last word selected: "last" typed replaces it and is found 1 of 1; opened a third time, Next searches the offered "last" once (1 of 1)
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-find.html
kit: cavekit-find-on-page.md R2, R5
calibrate top
sample before-menu 0,30,300,180
chrome appmenu
wait differs 0,30,300,180 before-menu 5
wait still 0,30,300,180 3
mark
chrome appmenu-find
expect keyboard up 8
type-keys zebra
wait line 'find .5 bytes. -> 1' 10
wait line 'find-result: {"index":1,"total":6' 10
mark
chrome find-next
wait line 'find: 2 of 6' 8
mark
chrome find-next
wait line 'find: 3 of 6' 8
mark
chrome find-next
wait line 'find: 4 of 6' 8
shoot dark-band
mark
chrome find-done
wait line 'find: cleared' 8
expect keyboard down 8
sample before-menu2 0,30,300,180
chrome appmenu
wait differs 0,30,300,180 before-menu2 5
wait still 0,30,300,180 3
chrome appmenu-find
expect keyboard up 8
shoot reopened
type-keys last
wait line 'find .4 bytes. -> 1' 10
wait line 'find-result: {"index":1,"total":1' 10
mark
chrome find-done
wait line 'find: cleared' 8
# opened a third time, "last" offered: Next searches it, once, and finds its one match (Codex review 2026-11-19: a step
# on top of the search skipped it). A tap on Next may take the focus from Mojo's field, so this comes after the typing.
sample before-menu3 0,30,300,180
chrome appmenu
wait differs 0,30,300,180 before-menu3 5
wait still 0,30,300,180 3
chrome appmenu-find
expect keyboard up 8
mark
chrome find-next
wait line 'find .4 bytes. -> 1' 8
wait line 'find-result: {"index":1,"total":1' 8
mark
chrome find-done
wait line 'find: cleared' 8
